  "worked_solution": "First, we use the identity $1+{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta ={csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta ,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta  & =[1+{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta ]+{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & ={csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor out ${csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta ,$ and we use the identity $1+{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta ={csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta $ again. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\,{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta  & ={csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta (1+{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta ) \\\\  & ={csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\,({csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta )\\, \\\\  & ={csc}^{4}\u2061\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
